						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <hr /> <p>Joined the site reluctantly, stay here reluctantly&#8230; I do a lot of things in life reluctantly.</p> <p>My works on the site, in (roughly) alphabetical order:</p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4528">Accendium Lucia (4528)</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/breathe-on-me">Breathe on Me</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/death-and-the-women">Death and the Women</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-5737">Entheogen (5737, 5000 contest entry)</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/et-sanabitur-anima-mea">et sanábitur ánima mea</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/ever-only-all">Ever, Only, All</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/i-say-this-that-you-suffer">i say this that you suffer</a></li> <li>Kadakúni <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/light-of-the-north">Light of the North, Or the Three Impossible Tasks of Te̮la</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/suekni-and-the-firebird">Sükni and the Firebird</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-catching-of-the-sun">The Catching of the Sun</a></li> </ul> </li> <li>Klavigar Character Studies <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/tuae">Tuae</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/such-a-world-as-this">Such A World As This</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/and-the-fact-it-rains">and the fact it rains</a></li> <li><a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/poisoned-honey">Poisoned Honey</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/elae">Elä</a></li> </ul> </li> <li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/unto-the-ages">Unto the Ages</a></li> </ul> <p>Commentary on said works, if you wish to read it:</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <ul> <li>Ever, Only, All: This was my first work on the site - literally 6000+ words recapping what I know about evolutionary history so far, as seen through Bronze Age eyes. Slightly Granola Sarkic, looking backwards.</li> <li>Kadakúni tales: Another internet writer, <a href="https://fialleril.tumblr.com/tagged/tatooine-slave-culture">fialleril</a>, developed an AU culture for Star Wars Tatooine. I decided that I wanted one of those things for myself, so I made one.</li> <li>Klavigar Character Studies: Second-person point of view is difficult to pull off, sometimes, but I do think it serves well for characters that occupy a somewhat mythical role, where first-person would feel too intimate and grandiose, while third-person would feel too cold and would not permit the reporting of private thoughts and feelings.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/oricat" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5199638&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606162312" alt="OriCat" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5199638)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/oricat" >OriCat</a></span></p> 
