&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.5em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 03:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.25em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conclusion of the Olivander Administration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following is part of an epistolary chain between outgoing Administrator H.V. Olivander and their designated successor, Michelle Wilkes. In compliance with the &lt;span style=&quot;color: red&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Atelis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt; object class, related communications not included in this document have been destroyed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FROM:&lt;/strong&gt; Administrator Emeritus, H.V. Olivander&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TO:&lt;/strong&gt; Administrator Pro Tempore, Michelle Wilkes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Michelle,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In my eighth and final missive, I counsel that we must think not of the self but of the greater whole when we lead this Foundation. The Ego must die if we are to live and continue our good works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You might never hear a member of leadership admit this out loud let alone to put the thought to paper, but we are all far better for the power of the Administrator being checked and balanced. The Administration and the O5 Council working in harmony to prevent any one person&#039;s ambition and agenda from compromising us all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My predecessor was fond of telling a story about the times he stood before the O5 Council. Imagine me, a Site Director who still felt wet behind the ears, sitting across the table from him receiving this wisdom as if I had any right to hear it. He decided his legacy was &#039;our&#039; legacy and the future became brighter for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I distinctly recall my own moment of realization, of crystallization, when the lesson he was trying to teach me finally made itself clear. Over the course of many long nights in the war room, we made one difficult decision after the other in order to resolve the Pripyat Incident. O5-3 was on my left, O5-11 further left of him, poring over new data with me from literally dusk until dawn. And then that fateful call came; I was handed the phone, given the news, and faced with a decision that only I was empowered to make.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The O5s said nothing out of respect to the moment. They all knew what their recommendations would be and they all knew what they hoped my answer would be before I had even finished processing the question. That was my chance; for them to know I could be the kind of leader they believed me to be. Pripyat resolved, and Olivander resolved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Although I go willingly into retirement, it is not without regret. My goals are not complete and the disease that now slowly claims my cognition and sanity ensures they will not be done by my own hand. The future belongs to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By the time you receive this letter my resignation will be complete and my duties as outgoing Administrator finalized. Tomorrow morning I am reporting to Site-00 in order to personally hand over my credentials, just as all those that came before me have done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All throughout the early years of my professional career I was convinced I would be different from the Administrators before me. However now, at the end, I realize it has been my life&#039;s most unapproachable honor to share in the same end. I wish nothing but the best for you and your tenure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good Luck,&lt;br /&gt;
H.V. Olivander&lt;br /&gt;
Former Administrator&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.5em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 04:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.25em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recovered Meeting Minutes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following transcription was recovered from the office of former Administrator H.V. Olivander along with a number of personal effects. The document has been authenticated against a number of internal controls, but due to the restrictions of the &lt;span style=&quot;color: red&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Atelis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt; object class, cannot be verified against certain administrative protocols. Therefore, the authenticity of this document is &lt;strong&gt;strongly believed&lt;/strong&gt; but not unequivocally accepted. Proceed with caution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;border: solid 2px #000000; padding: 1px 15px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.5em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MEETING MINUTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;lt;The meeting begins as all members of the O5 Council simultaneously take their seats around a large, rectangular, stone table. The center of the table is lit by conical, hanging lights and the identity of each O5 member is reduced to a silhouette with a nameplate sat in front of them. These nameplates bear title only. &amp;quot;O5-1&amp;quot; stands and speaks first.&amp;gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-1:&lt;/strong&gt; Friends. I mustn&#039;t stay long. I just had to see you. &lt;em&gt;&amp;lt;They then sit&amp;gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-5:&lt;/strong&gt; Man must be made to receive without pride, to let go without attachment. True improvement lies with finding contentment in being thought foolish and stupid. In finding this success, they must be challenged to die. Ego must die or nothing of heaven can live within. The stars burn brightly to shine on us, not on you. Love outlasts death. The stream feeds the ocean feeds the stream.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-9:&lt;/strong&gt; My children believe I am God.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-7:&lt;/strong&gt; No ceremonies are necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-10:&lt;/strong&gt; Body is purified by water. Ego by tears.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All Members In Unison:&lt;/strong&gt; We agree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-1:&lt;/strong&gt; Order. We will now hear new business. The chair recognizes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-6:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;&amp;lt;Stands up&amp;gt;&lt;/em&gt; Green should smell more tranquil. Instead, it just smells rotten. &lt;em&gt;&amp;lt;Sits&amp;gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-2, O5-3, O5-4 in Unison:&lt;/strong&gt; We agree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-11:&lt;/strong&gt; I call the question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-1:&lt;/strong&gt; Order. There can be no debate. The vote carries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All Members In Unison:&lt;/strong&gt; We agree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-13:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;&amp;lt;Stands up&amp;gt;&lt;/em&gt; Administrator is made of old bones. It is time. We cannot put them to the left.&lt;em&gt;&amp;lt;Sits&amp;gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-12:&lt;/strong&gt; He will do as told.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-8, O5-9, O5-10:&lt;/strong&gt; We agree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-7:&lt;/strong&gt; I call the question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-1:&lt;/strong&gt; Order. There can be no vote. The debate carries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All Members In Unison:&lt;/strong&gt; We agree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O5-1:&lt;/strong&gt; Order. We adjourn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.5em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum 05:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.25em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Memorandum of Understanding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following epistolary chain is an exchange between Administrator Wilkes and SCP-001 which began shortly after she assumed full control of her new position. This chain of communication is understood to be complete. Any additional communications taking place chronologically after the final noted entry are to be destroyed in compliance with &lt;span style=&quot;color: red&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Atelis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt; protocols.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FROM:&lt;/strong&gt; O5 Council&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TO:&lt;/strong&gt; Administrator Wilkes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Administrator,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We approach our first occasion for your resolve to be tested. Please report for a briefing on &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/tuesday-canceled|&quot;&gt;Tuesday&lt;/a&gt; at 19:00 hours and we will bring you up to speed on the matters at hand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Formally,&lt;br /&gt;
O5 Council&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FROM:&lt;/strong&gt; Administrator Wilkes&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TO:&lt;/strong&gt; O5 Council&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Council,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please have all project briefings and mission briefs you intend to cover sent to my office as soon as possible so we can make the most efficient use of our time. I am looking forward to hitting the ground running and working with all of you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sincerely,&lt;br /&gt;
Administrator Wilkes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FROM:&lt;/strong&gt; THOSE WHO KNOW BETTER&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TO:&lt;/strong&gt; ADMINISTRATOR WILKES&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ADMINISTRATOR,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:1.25em;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROPOSAL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
UNDERSTANDING IS A PROCESS. WE GUIDE.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VOTES FOR:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
All&lt;/p&gt;
