					<![CDATA[
						 <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /></p> <div style="text-align: right;"> <div class="creditRate"> <div class="rateBox"> <div class="rate-box-with-credit-button"> <div class="creditButton"> <p><a class="fa fa-info" href="#u-credit-view"></a></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div style="clear:both;"></div> <div id="u-credit-view"> <div class="fader"> <p><iframe src="http://scp-jp-sandbox3.wdfiles.com/local--code/credit%3Abackmodule/1" align="" frameborder="" height="" scrolling="" width="" class="" style=""></iframe></p> </div> <div class="modalcontainer"> <div class="modalbox"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h2><span>Info</span></h2> </div> <hr /> <div class="credit first"> <p><iframe src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--code/info%3Astyle/3" align="" frameborder="" height="" scrolling="" width="" class="close-credits" style="height:2em;margin: 0;padding: 0;border: 0;background: transparent;"></iframe></p> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /></p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>SCP-001 Dr. Eates' Proposal<br /> &quot;Facio, Ergo Sum&quot;</strong></p> <p>-or-</p> <p><strong>&quot;Death of the Ego&quot;</strong><br /> by: <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2104082&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606162312" alt="ManyMeats" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2104082)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" >ManyMeats</a></span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/manymeats">★ ManyMeats Author Page ★</a></p> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="credit-back" style="text-align: center;"> <p><iframe src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--code/info%3Astyle/2" align="" frameborder="" height="" scrolling="no" width="" class="" style="height:2em;width: 100%;margin: 0;padding: 0;border: 0;background: transparent;"></iframe></p> </div> <div class="creditBottomRate" style="position:relative;height:30px;"> <div style="text-align: center; top: 0px;"></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span> <div style="background: url(http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/the-great-hippo/scp_trans.png) center no-repeat ; float: center; border: solid 2px #000000; padding: 1px 15px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h1><span>WARNING:</span></h1> <h4><span>CONTINUED ACCESS TO THIS FILE MANDATES THE USE OF THE COGITO PROTOCOL. ALL CONSENTING PARTIES WILL HAVE TEN(10) MINUTES TO RESPOND BEFORE AUTOMATIC VOTE FAILURE. A SUPER-MAJORITY IS REQUIRED TO PROCEED. UNAUTHORIZED INDIVIDUALS ATTEMPTING TO INITIATE A VOTE WILL BE NEUTRALIZED.</span></h4> <h4><span>THERE WILL BE NO ADDITIONAL WARNINGS.</span></h4> </div> <br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></div> <br /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h4><span>PING RESPONSES RECEIVED: [15/15]</span></h4> <h4><span>QUORUM ESTABLISHED</span></h4> <p>.<br /> .<br /> .</p> <h4><span>INITIATING BALLOT PRESENTATION</span></h4> <p>.</p> <h5><span><strong>[6/15] VOTES RECEIVED</strong></span></h5> <h5><span><strong>[8/15] VOTES RECEIVED</strong></span></h5> <h5><span><strong>[15/15] VOTES RECEIVED</strong></span></h5> <h5><span><strong>TALLYING&#8230;</strong></span></h5> <p>.<br /> .<br /> .</p> <h4><span><strong>VOTE RESULT: <span style="color: green">SUCCESS</span></strong></span></h4> <h4><span><strong>YOU MAY PROCEED</strong></span></h4> <p>.<br /> .<br /> .</p> </div> <br /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[**COGITO&nbsp;PROTOCOL&nbsp;CONFIRMED:&nbsp;ACCESS&nbsp;FILE&nbsp;SCP-001**]</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[TERMINATE&nbsp;SESSION&nbsp;AND&nbsp;LOG&nbsp;OUT.]</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <hr /> <hr /> <div style="text-align: left;"> <table style="border: none; width: 100%;"> <tr> <td><span style="font-size:125%;"><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-001</span></td> <td style="text-align: right;"><span style="font-size:125%;"><span style="color: #990000"><strong>Level 5/001</strong></span></span></td> </tr> <tr> <td><span style="font-size:125%;"><strong>Object Class:</strong> Atelis</span></td> <td style="text-align: right;"><span style="font-size:125%;"><span style="color: #990000"><strong>Classified</strong></span></span></td> </tr> </table> <hr /> <hr /> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>CLASSIFICATION NOTICE:</strong></p> <hr /> <p>As the containment of SCP-001 requires an incomplete understanding of its purpose, parameters, and function, the Classification Committee has voted to establish the <strong>Atelis</strong> object class. Atelis denotes an object that requires the intentional ignorance of related matters, including secondary and tertiary concerns, in order to be contained. Any objects or personnel separated by two degrees or fewer from an Atelis-class object are to be flagged and processed in compliance with established protocols.</p> </blockquote> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> Secure Area-00 has been established around the space believed to contain SCP-001 and classified Level 6/Cosmic Secret. The coordinates of Secure Area-00 are asymmetrically stored in the cranial implants of 15 selected members of Foundation Leadership, considered from a pool of Ethics Committee members and Site Directors. Data contained within these implants may only be decrypted by a super-majority vote (80%). Candidates are unaware of their status as voters until and unless a vote is called.</p> <p>In the event that the cipher becomes compromised or a cranial implant fails to ping, COGITO.aic will generate a new cryptographic protocol and distribute it to a new group of candidates. After the protocol has been updated, COGITO.aic will self-delete in order to purge the knowledge of Secure Area-00 and a new 'AIC' will be cloned from the template and promoted.</p> <p>No access to Secure Area-00 is permitted at any time for any reason. All relevant site operation protocols, internal and external defenses, schematics, contingencies, and other related information have been expunged.</p> <p>Per the constraints of the <span style="color: red"><strong>Atelis</strong></span> object class, under no circumstances are Site Directors or members of the Ethics Committee allowed access to any portion of this file unless a decryption vote is taking place.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-001 is the absence of the O5 Council. In spite of all historical evidence detailing the activities of the O5 Council, the identities and histories of its members, and the existence of complex support structures directly and indirectly attached to the object, the O5 Council does not definitively exist.</p> <p>All contemporary records relating to the O5 Council - other than those contained in this file - are believed to be either fabricated by personnel under the influence of, or directly manifested by, SCP-001 itself. All data related to the orchestration of these events has been expunged in accordance with <span style="color: red"><strong>Atelis</strong></span> protocols.</p> </div> <hr /> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>Addendum 01:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;"><strong>Conclusion of the Cohen Administration</strong></span></p> <hr /> <div style="text-align: left;"> <p>The following epistolary chain began at the end of Administrator Cohen's tenure as he formally transitioned duties and classified materials to his designated successor, H.V. Olivander. While this chain of communication was originally designated as complete, there were a number of correspondences between involved parties which may have contained additional information or context on this matter. These records have been destroyed in accordance with <span style="color: red"><strong>Atelis</strong></span> protocols.</p> <p>This chain of communication is the earliest known reference to the O5 Council in any recorded fashion.</p> <p>Should any additional records be discovered pertaining to this matter, personnel are instructed to immediately destroy these records and contact Internal Security using challenge response &quot;Carthage&quot;.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> Administrator Emeritus, William Cohen<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> Administrator Pro Tempore, H.V. Olivander</p> <hr /> <p>Harold,</p> <p>In my fifth and final missive I would speak frankly with you about the company you keep. Trust is very important and as much as any competent administrator or leader should trust themselves, they should also trust that their interests are well represented.</p> <p>This disease that clings to my mind like tar has caused me to no longer trust myself, and so, I pass this knowledge on to you while it remains untainted.</p> <p>I remember the day I was first invited to speak to the Council. O5-1 approached me beforehand, sat me down, and told me that they felt I was going to make an error in judgment; that my priorities were wrong. It was tough to swallow but the seriousness of their voice and the passion of their rhetoric made it clear that we were on the same side. That we wanted the same thing. I didn't know what to do but their counsel helped me find the truth through the fog. In the middle of the night, standing at the head of the table of the O5 Council, deep in the bunker of Site-00, I addressed them. If only they knew how my knees quaked the entire time I spoke.</p> <p>After my briefing had concluded, the O5s approved of and accepted my recommendation unanimously. Ironically, I don't remember what that briefing was even about anymore, but I remember the professional satisfaction that followed. It still comes to me in my idle thoughts much like my wedding day, or the very first Anomalous Incident I responded to. I can touch that memory in the space of my mind with the same certainty as I recall my own name.</p> <p>Yet in spite of this I must assert with equal clarity that this meeting never took place.</p> <p>Terms like 'Overseer' and Site-00 were never more than a concept, a dream. Never brick and mortar. Yet I remember. I've been there. I've spoken to them and they've spoken to me. At this point in my life I fear what I know almost as much as I fear what I have forgotten.</p> <p>By the time you receive this letter, my retirement will be complete. As my final professional act, I will report to Site-00 tomorrow morning to hand in my credentials and express my appreciation one last time to those who mentored me for so long.</p> <p>The Foundation is in good hands.</p> <p>Best wishes,<br /> William Cohen<br /> Former Administrator</p> </blockquote> </div> <hr /> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>Addendum 02:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;"><strong>Recovered Documentation</strong></span></p> <hr /> <div style="text-align: left;"> <p>The following set of documents are the earliest known communications created and distributed by the O5 Council. Due to inconsistent records management policies between administrations, it is unknown if earlier documentation exists.</p> <p>Should any additional records be discovered pertaining to this matter, personnel are instructed to cease reading these records and contact Internal Security using challenge response &quot;Troy&quot;.</p> <div id="wiki-tabview-bac3a9677e7d847e3a98edb3fb4f415c" class="yui-navset"> <ul class="yui-nav"> <li class="selected"><a href="javascript:;"><em>MEMORANDUM 1</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>MEMORANDUM 2</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>MEMORANDUM 3</em></a></li> </ul> <div class="yui-content"> <div id="wiki-tab-0-0"> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> O5 COUNCIL, ET AL<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> ADMINISTRATION<br /> <strong>PURPOSE:</strong> MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING</p> <hr /> <p>ADMINISTRATOR COHEN,</p> <p>THIS IS A CLOSED SYSTEM.<br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /></p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;">THE LEFT-HAND PATH AWAITS US</span></p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> All</p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> None</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: green">APPROVED</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> O5 COUNCIL, ET AL<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> ETHICS COMMITTEE<br /> <strong>PURPOSE:</strong> MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING</p> <hr /> <p>COUNCILMEN &amp; COUNCILWOMEN,</p> <p>WE INSTRUCT YOU TO CONTRADICT YOURSELF.<br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /></p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;">A CHURCH IS A HOSPITAL FOR SINNERS</span></p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> All</p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> None</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: green">APPROVED</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> O5 COUNCIL, ET AL<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> OVERWATCH COMMAND<br /> <strong>PURPOSE:</strong> MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING</p> <hr /> <p>COLLEAGUES,</p> <p>YOU WILL DO NOTHING BECAUSE THERE IS NOTHING YOU HAVE NOT ALREADY DONE.<br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /></p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;">THEY SHALL BEAT THEIR SWORDS TO PLOWSHARES</span></p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> All</p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> None</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: green">APPROVED</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>Addendum 03:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;"><strong>Conclusion of the Olivander Administration</strong></span></p> </div> <hr /> <p>The following is part of an epistolary chain between outgoing Administrator H.V. Olivander and their designated successor, Michelle Wilkes. In compliance with the <span style="color: red"><strong>Atelis</strong></span> object class, related communications not included in this document have been destroyed.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> Administrator Emeritus, H.V. Olivander<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> Administrator Pro Tempore, Michelle Wilkes</p> <hr /> <p>Michelle,</p> <p>In my eighth and final missive, I counsel that we must think not of the self but of the greater whole when we lead this Foundation. The Ego must die if we are to live and continue our good works.</p> <p>You might never hear a member of leadership admit this out loud let alone to put the thought to paper, but we are all far better for the power of the Administrator being checked and balanced. The Administration and the O5 Council working in harmony to prevent any one person's ambition and agenda from compromising us all.</p> <p>My predecessor was fond of telling a story about the times he stood before the O5 Council. Imagine me, a Site Director who still felt wet behind the ears, sitting across the table from him receiving this wisdom as if I had any right to hear it. He decided his legacy was 'our' legacy and the future became brighter for it.</p> <p>I distinctly recall my own moment of realization, of crystallization, when the lesson he was trying to teach me finally made itself clear. Over the course of many long nights in the war room, we made one difficult decision after the other in order to resolve the Pripyat Incident. O5-3 was on my left, O5-11 further left of him, poring over new data with me from literally dusk until dawn. And then that fateful call came; I was handed the phone, given the news, and faced with a decision that only I was empowered to make.</p> <p>The O5s said nothing out of respect to the moment. They all knew what their recommendations would be and they all knew what they hoped my answer would be before I had even finished processing the question. That was my chance; for them to know I could be the kind of leader they believed me to be. Pripyat resolved, and Olivander resolved.</p> <p>Although I go willingly into retirement, it is not without regret. My goals are not complete and the disease that now slowly claims my cognition and sanity ensures they will not be done by my own hand. The future belongs to you.</p> <p>By the time you receive this letter my resignation will be complete and my duties as outgoing Administrator finalized. Tomorrow morning I am reporting to Site-00 in order to personally hand over my credentials, just as all those that came before me have done.</p> <p>All throughout the early years of my professional career I was convinced I would be different from the Administrators before me. However now, at the end, I realize it has been my life's most unapproachable honor to share in the same end. I wish nothing but the best for you and your tenure.</p> <p>Good Luck,<br /> H.V. Olivander<br /> Former Administrator</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>Addendum 04:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;"><strong>Recovered Meeting Minutes</strong></span></p> </div> <hr /> <p>The following transcription was recovered from the office of former Administrator H.V. Olivander along with a number of personal effects. The document has been authenticated against a number of internal controls, but due to the restrictions of the <span style="color: red"><strong>Atelis</strong></span> object class, cannot be verified against certain administrative protocols. Therefore, the authenticity of this document is <strong>strongly believed</strong> but not unequivocally accepted. Proceed with caution.</p> <div style="border: solid 2px #000000; padding: 1px 15px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>MEETING MINUTES</strong></span></p> </div> <hr /> <p><em>&lt;The meeting begins as all members of the O5 Council simultaneously take their seats around a large, rectangular, stone table. The center of the table is lit by conical, hanging lights and the identity of each O5 member is reduced to a silhouette with a nameplate sat in front of them. These nameplates bear title only. &quot;O5-1&quot; stands and speaks first.&gt;</em></p> <p><strong>O5-1:</strong> Friends. I mustn't stay long. I just had to see you. <em>&lt;They then sit&gt;</em></p> <p><strong>O5-5:</strong> Man must be made to receive without pride, to let go without attachment. True improvement lies with finding contentment in being thought foolish and stupid. In finding this success, they must be challenged to die. Ego must die or nothing of heaven can live within. The stars burn brightly to shine on us, not on you. Love outlasts death. The stream feeds the ocean feeds the stream.</p> <p><strong>O5-9:</strong> My children believe I am God.</p> <p><strong>O5-7:</strong> No ceremonies are necessary.</p> <p><strong>O5-10:</strong> Body is purified by water. Ego by tears.</p> <p><strong>All Members In Unison:</strong> We agree.</p> <p><strong>O5-1:</strong> Order. We will now hear new business. The chair recognizes.</p> <p><strong>O5-6:</strong> <em>&lt;Stands up&gt;</em> Green should smell more tranquil. Instead, it just smells rotten. <em>&lt;Sits&gt;</em></p> <p><strong>O5-2, O5-3, O5-4 in Unison:</strong> We agree.</p> <p><strong>O5-11:</strong> I call the question.</p> <p><strong>O5-1:</strong> Order. There can be no debate. The vote carries.</p> <p><strong>All Members In Unison:</strong> We agree.</p> <p><strong>O5-13:</strong> <em>&lt;Stands up&gt;</em> Administrator is made of old bones. It is time. We cannot put them to the left.<em>&lt;Sits&gt;</em></p> <p><strong>O5-12:</strong> He will do as told.</p> <p><strong>O5-8, O5-9, O5-10:</strong> We agree.</p> <p><strong>O5-7:</strong> I call the question.</p> <p><strong>O5-1:</strong> Order. There can be no vote. The debate carries.</p> <p><strong>All Members In Unison:</strong> We agree.</p> <p><strong>O5-1:</strong> Order. We adjourn.</p> </div> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>Addendum 05:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;"><strong>Memorandum of Understanding</strong></span></p> </div> <hr /> <p>The following epistolary chain is an exchange between Administrator Wilkes and SCP-001 which began shortly after she assumed full control of her new position. This chain of communication is understood to be complete. Any additional communications taking place chronologically after the final noted entry are to be destroyed in compliance with <span style="color: red"><strong>Atelis</strong></span> protocols.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> O5 Council<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> Administrator Wilkes</p> <hr /> <p>Administrator,</p> <p>We approach our first occasion for your resolve to be tested. Please report for a briefing on <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/tuesday-canceled|">Tuesday</a> at 19:00 hours and we will bring you up to speed on the matters at hand.</p> <p>Formally,<br /> O5 Council</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> Administrator Wilkes<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> O5 Council</p> <hr /> <p>Council,</p> <p>Please have all project briefings and mission briefs you intend to cover sent to my office as soon as possible so we can make the most efficient use of our time. I am looking forward to hitting the ground running and working with all of you.</p> <p>Sincerely,<br /> Administrator Wilkes</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> THOSE WHO KNOW BETTER<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> ADMINISTRATOR WILKES</p> <hr /> <p>ADMINISTRATOR,</p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.25em;"><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong></span><br /> UNDERSTANDING IS A PROCESS. WE GUIDE.</p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> All</p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> None</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: green">ACCEPT</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> Administrator Wilkes<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> O5 Council</p> <hr /> <p>Council,</p> <p>I am certainly willing to work with you on whatever matters might be on our agenda, but I need to do so from a position of preparedness and strength. Send those materials immediately. Please.</p> <p>Administrator Wilkes</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> THE COUNCIL IN ITS AUTHORITY<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> ADMINISTRATOR XXXX</p> <hr /> <p>ADMINISTRATOR,</p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong><br /> SEEING IS BELIEVING. WE WILL SHOW YOU.</p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> All</p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> None</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: green">ACKNOWLEDGE</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> Administrator Wilkes<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> O5 Council</p> <hr /> <p>Council,</p> <p>Your approach is both personally insulting and professionally unacceptable. I have been transitioning many duties from my predecessor, reading notes and past minutes, assessing the strengths and leverage of each business unit and department, and otherwise readying myself for these matters for the better part of a year. If you are not going to demonstrate the courtesy and care due my station, my person, and the Foundation then I will do what I must without you.</p> <p>Tantrums are the last thing I expected from this body. Deference? What about cooperation? This is the last olive branch I am going to offer you. I trust you to do the right thing but I will not allow my previous loyalties or the run-away sense of nostalgia that surrounds my office to cause me to be derelict or negligent in my duties.</p> <p>I await your answer,<br /> Administrator Wilkes</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> THE COUNCIL IN EVEN GREATER AUTHORITY<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> ADMINISTRATOR NASCENT</p> <hr /> <p>ADMINISTRATOR,</p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong><br /> REPORT TO SITE-00 FOR NEW EMPLOYEE ORIENTATION</p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> All</p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> None</p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: green">NOW</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> Administrator Wilkes<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> O5 Council</p> <hr /> <p>Council,</p> <p>No.</p> <p>Administrator Wilkes</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> THE ONLY FRIEND YOU HAVE<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> MERAKI</p> <hr /> <p>AD MIN,</p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong><br /> ?YOU ARE READY?</p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> <span style="font-size:1.5em;"><span style="color: red"><strong>NONE</strong></span></span></p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> <span style="font-size:1.5em;"><span style="color: red"><strong>ALL</strong></span></span></p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: red">FACE IT</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> The Administrator<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> O5 Council</p> <hr /> <p>Council,</p> <p>I was told I would be faced with the hardest of decisions from the beginning of my tenure and that the spirit and integrity with which I faced these challenges would set the tone for years. We may either rise to meet the occasion of a challenge&#8230;or we may run from what duty might demand, retreating within procedures, votes, and protocols.</p> <p>I choose the former.</p> <p>I choose to act to protect this Foundation.</p> <p>In my authority as Administrator and as designated by the Charter for the Foundation, I hereby dissolve the authority of the body known as the &quot;O5 Council&quot; effective immediately.</p> <p>Facio, ergo sum.</p> <p>The Administrator</p> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p><strong>FROM:</strong> O5 Council<br /> <strong>TO:</strong> Administrator Michelle Wilkes</p> <hr /> <p>Administrator,</p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>PROPOSAL:</strong><br /> YOU ARE READY.</p> <p><strong>VOTES FOR:</strong><br /> All</p> <p><strong>VOTES AGAINST:</strong><br /> <span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>None</strong></span></p> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <th>STATUS</th> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><span style="color: green">APPROVED</span></strong></td> </tr> </table> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><span style="font-size:1.5em;"><strong>Addendum 06:</strong></span><br /> <span style="font-size:1.25em;"><strong>Object Classification Memo</strong></span></p> </div> <hr /> <p>The following memorandum was issued by Administrator Wilkes and attached to this document along with the Administrator's personal file-lock. No further changes to this document, even for matters of contextual or procedural clarification, are permitted without the express lifting of this personal file-lock.</p> <div style="border: solid 2px #000000; padding: 1px 15px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);"> <p><strong>ATTN: CLASSIFICATION COMMITTEE</strong><br /> <strong>FROM: ADMINISTRATOR WILKES</strong></p> <hr /> <p>Colleagues,</p> <p>In order to preserve the authority and autonomy of our organization, its sub-divisions, and its appointed personnel, I must declare my first and hopefully only unilateral action as Administrator of the Foundation. You are hereby mandated to construct a new object class and all contingent protocols as advocated by the attached documentation.</p> <p>While the authority to name this class is at your discretion I offer as a nominee <span style="color: red"><strong>ἀτελής</strong></span> (a-te-lis), a Greek word meaning an unfulfilled or incomplete understanding. The merits of this suggestion should be clear from the attached briefing. Implementation will begin as soon as you ratify the object class.</p> <p>I am making you complicit in our future.</p> <p>First, I'm sorry.</p> <p>Second, You're welcome.</p> <p>Good Luck,<br /> Administrator Wilkes</p> </div> </div> <br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <hr /> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/manymeats">Dr. Eates Personnel File</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2104082&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606162312" alt="ManyMeats" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2104082)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/manymeats" >ManyMeats</a></span></p> 
