&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #43d738&quot;&gt;(E)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/a-dime-a-dozen&quot;&gt;A Dime A Dozen: An Essay On Critiquing Ideas, Community, and Making The Most Out Of Nothing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: RockTeethMothEyes provides advice on how to approach critiquing different kinds of concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #43d738&quot;&gt;(E)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/an-exercise-in-narrative-based-scps&quot;&gt;An exercise in narrative based SCPs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Leveritas presents an overview on some ways to approach SCPs with narratives/backstories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #43d738&quot;&gt;(E)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/shanor-ideas-essay&quot;&gt;Conceptual Critique and Burnout, A Guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Shanor provides tips on how to critique concepts and how to avoid critiquer burnout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #43d738&quot;&gt;(E)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/how-to-become-a-better-critic&quot;&gt;How to Become a Better Critic&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Things to keep in mind when leaving reviewer comments and feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
